    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d971">

                <pb facs="0922" n="910" sameAs="frus:frus1943v04/pg910"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.24/1160: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Minister Resident in Saudi Arabia</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Moose</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-11-08T19:00:00-04:00">November 8, 1943—7
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>97. With reference to the British plan to supply Saudi Arabia with the military
                    equipment described in Department’s 92, October 23,<anchor n="4"
                        xml:id="d971-f1"/> please inform us whether Ibn Saud or other Saudi Arabian
                    officials approached the British in regard to such supplies and, if so, the
                    circumstances under which the approach was made. Please state also whether any
                    of this equipment has been delivered by the British.<anchor n="4a"
                        xml:id="d971-f2"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stettinius</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d971-f1" n="4" xml:id="d971-f1-content">
                <p>See footnote 99, <ref target="#pg908">p. 908</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d971-f2" n="4a" xml:id="d971-f2-content">
                <p>For a British report regarding the approach by Mr. Moose to the Saudi Arabian
                    Government pursuant to this instruction, and comment by Mr. Moose thereon, see
                        <ref target="frus1943CairoTehran#pg_378">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, The Conferences at Cairo and
                        Tehran, 1943, pp. 378</ref> and <ref target="frus1943CairoTehran#pg_447"
                        >447</ref>; for the Minister Resident’s reply to the Department on November
                    19, see telegram No. 189, <ref target="#pg912">p. 912</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
